  "limits": [
    "Prepared families must be already oriented polynomial curves with exact common weights and unit domains. Station lists increase from 0 to 1 and match the opposite-family counts. Existing 2-to-32 curves per family, degree 16, 128 controls per curve and 2048 total-control caps remain. Failed or inconclusive prescribed-chart proofs reject without a general pullback substitution.",
    "This is a construction primitive, not a NetworkSrf command or general smoothness/topology guarantee. Complete source-image correspondence does not prove injectivity, topology, symmetric distance or Rhino interior fitting. Curve refits retain their adaptive sampled fit policy.",
    "The common-station cubic fixture retains simple knots and C2 continuity; its global scalar-map policy remains unselected and still fails the 1e-6 Rhino interior query comparison. All four independent candidates remain unqualified.",
    "Reference-derived isocurve reconstruction deliberately uses curves extracted from the saved Rhino tensor. Its passing 25-point comparison and the sampled Gordon residual isolate construction on one fixture; neither qualifies independent family fitting or proves continuous surface separation.",
    "Twelve fresh standalone public Fit results support sampled midpoint-parameter diagnostics only. They do not establish broader FitCrv parity or identify Rhino internal algorithms. No proprietary implementation was inspected.",
    "SMLib, SM_API and adapter archives are instrumented by AddressSanitizer. Rust and separately bundled dependencies are not separately instrumented; leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks are disabled. No runtime/performance qualification is claimed."
  ],
